 "chunking": {
  "name": "Sentry Eye SD-5 Camera Deadbolt",
  "sku": "SKU-0498",
  "words": 219,
  "fragments": [
   "Some homeowners want to see who is at the door before they open it, and the Brightwell Sentry Eye SD-5 puts a camera directly into the deadbolt housing. The exterior panel holds a 2-megapixel wide-angle lens with a 150-degree field of view, infrared night vision up to 25 feet, and a motion-triggered recording mode. The lock body is zinc alloy with a satin nickel finish, and the bolt throws a full one inch. You can unlock using a fingerprint reader on the exterior, a keypad with up to 50 codes, or the Brightwell app, which streams live video over Wi-Fi. Clips are saved to a microSD card of up to 128 gigabytes or to an optional cloud subscription. The SD-5 relies on a rechargeable battery pack that lasts about three months between charges, and a USB-C port makes charging simple. Video quality may decline in very low light or when the Wi-Fi signal is weak. Keep the lens clean by wiping it with a soft microfiber cloth, avoiding harsh chemicals. Check the microSD card every few months to confirm recording continues. Brightwell offers a two-year warranty on the lock and a one-year warranty on the camera module. The SD-5 suits front doors with reliable internet service, and its camera is meant to supplement, not replace, conventional home security practices."
  ]
 },
